iv. non-publication of prospectus by the institution, in accordance with the provisions of these Regulations;
v. publication by the institution of any information in the prospectus, which is false or misleading, and not based on facts;
vi. withholding of, or refusal to return, any document in the form of certificates of degree, diploma or any other award or
other document deposited by a student for the purpose of seeking admission in such institution, with a view to induce or
compel such student to pay any fee or fees in respect of any course or program of study which such student does not
intend to pursue;
vii. demand of money in excess of that specified to be charged in the declared admission policyof the institution;
viii. violation, by the institution, of any law for the time being in force in regard to reservation of seats in admission to
different category of students;
